  "summary": "The study compares four Ti3C2Tx-derived electrodes: untreated multilayer Ti3C2Tx, KOH\u2013Ti3C2, KOAc\u2013Ti3C2, and DMSO-delaminated d-Ti3C2. KOH and KOAc treatments chemically intercalate potassium salts and replace fluorine-rich surfaces with oxygen-containing groups, whereas DMSO yields a thin delaminated MXene paper. The headline d-Ti3C2 electrode delivered 520 F\u00b7cm\u22123 and 325 F\u00b7g\u22121 at 2 mV\u00b7s\u22121 in 1 M H2SO4; it also gave 415 F\u00b7cm\u22123 at 5 A\u00b7g\u22121. KOH\u2013Ti3C2 delivered 215 F\u00b7cm\u22123 at 5 A\u00b7g\u22121, while exact capacitance values for untreated Ti3C2Tx and KOAc\u2013Ti3C2 are not printed in the supplied text."
